==Battleground==
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**6 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Midnite D.|Midnite Ds]] spawn, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
**2 [[Beefcake Cat (Enemy)|Beefcake Cats]] spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Do not underestimate this stage. Highly buffed Aku Gories supported by 2 Beefcake Cats can easily kill you. Try to save money from the beginning and then spawn high DPS units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks Cat]] to take them down. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] is highly recommended to use in the start to help easily build up money thanks to the technique you can use with him to kill the Aku Doges. [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Tathagata Cat]] is going to be your main proc unit against the Beefcake Cats because he can outrange them and have a constant slow on them. [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] are very good with dealing with the enemies, specifically Professor A. If the Beefcake Cats manage to die early bring a unit that can outrange Professor A. like [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]]. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] is also necessary to kill the Midnite Ds.

